{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792872332,"nonce":"vVlu8I+mbXRHwy85HzTadOnSWAU=","message":"Implemented group-only CSS opacity cache patching, grouped with its direct/compositor fallback safeguards.\n\napply_css_deltas validates every changed opacity before mutating any cache record, primitive or group command. A missing index, out-of-range index or non-Push command returns Bail and clears damage metadata. Valid group opacity updates preserve child colors, including 0 -\u003e nonzero recovery. Keyframe opacity takes precedence over transition opacity, with transition fallback when the playing animation does not supply opacity. The obsolete per-primitive alpha-ratio branch and zero-ratio rejection are removed.\n\nThe compositor now invalidates its static layer after a rejected CSS patch or re-emission so ordinary cache replay cannot bypass the required full walk. The direct renderer has no CSS patch pass, so active CSS (including pending final property writes reported by css_has_active) conservatively disables its binding-only fast path. Its full walk still uses existing promotion/bake hash policy. Public CSS/motion promotion guards are unchanged.\n\nNegative control: all four new tests failed before the production change. At the first 1 -\u003e 0.5 frame, compositor overlap (55,55) was [64,128,64,255] and direct overlap stayed [0,255,0,255], both expected [0,128,128,255]. Valid-group recovery from zero returned Bail, and missing-group opacity was accepted. Log: /private/tmp/blinc-css-opacity-negative.log.\n\nFinal scoped validation:\n- Four new opacity_groups_css tests pass normally and with both storage flags forced off (data textures). Public direct/compositor frames cover playing keyframes and transitions, starting at opacity one without a group and changing through 0.5, 0, 0.75, 1, 0.5, with unchanged-frame replay and no manual cache invalidation. A constant background-color property keeps these fixtures non-promoted.\n- The API guard test uses two real CSS records and poisons the later record's command metadata. Missing index, out-of-range index and Pop index all reject before the earlier valid record is patched. Primitive bytes, command data and all paint baselines stay unchanged; stale damage is cleared. Both animation and transition stores are covered.\n- The API group test patches 0.5 -\u003e 0 -\u003e 0.75 -\u003e 1 -\u003e 0.25, verifies full-opacity child bytes stay unchanged and checks animation/transition precedence and fallback.\n- Nine adjacent controls passed normally: existing opacity_groups cases excluding opacity_groups_css (3), composite scratch CSS index guard (1), promoted-root CSS opacity live blit (1), retained foreground CSS repaint (1), dynamic CSS index guard (1), static group suppression of CSS child promotion (1), and dynamic binding zero recovery (1).\n- Total: 13 selected tests normally, with the four new tests also passing in forced data-texture mode. CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, fallback capacities 1024, offscreen only. Touched-file rustfmt, diff checks and bounded production-module sizes pass. Temporary GPU capability overrides restored; no GPU source diff.\n\nLogs: /private/tmp/blinc-css-opacity-normal.log, /private/tmp/blinc-css-opacity-normal-opacity_groups.log, six /private/tmp/blinc-css-opacity-normal-* control logs, and /private/tmp/blinc-css-opacity-dt-opacity_groups_css.log. Driver: /private/tmp/blinc_css_opacity_modes.py. No workspace/DSL/docs/platform or unrelated gates.\n\nPerformance: opacity preflight scans existing CSS paint records without allocating. Direct active CSS frames now require full walks rather than binding-only replay; an ungrouped compositor opacity change requires a full paint to establish its group, after which represented opacity can patch. No shader, GPU layout, new resource type or timing/memory benchmark. No browser/mobile or scheduler interpolation claim.\n\nRemaining parent scope includes cross-stream isolation, separately collected text/SVG/ImageElement and GPU pass/mesh output, named Sample and other mixed-cache ownership. This slice covers existing CSS paint records; compositor nodes absent from the recorded paint, including fully transparent initial frames, are not covered. No general missing-record or animation-start/stop lifecycle claim. No push.","files":null}]}